# pico-dgx-ds4 — cp .env.example .env (start.sh and stop.sh load it; .env is
# gitignored). This is the whole surface: everything not here is a default in
# start.sh, and a default can still be overridden from the environment
# (DSGB10_PORT, WAIT_TIMEOUT, ...) if you ever need to.
#
# The fleet file: the rank list, the boxes' addresses and where each rank keeps
# its files.
FLEET=./ds41f-4xgx10-switchless/fleet/homelab.conf
#
# The other boxes, if the fleet file does not exist yet: rank 0 is the head (this
# box) and each target is one more rank, so this list IS the rank count — there
# is no TP to set. One target cuts and installs two ranks, three cut four; the
# engine loads four (engine/common/tp.h).
# WORKERS="olyno@10.0.0.4 olyno@10.0.0.3 olyno@10.0.0.2"
#
# 1: serve without a bearer key (loopback or a trusted network only).
# DSGB10_NO_AUTH=1
#
# Direct ring: 2 when every rank reaches every other in one hop (one switch).
# DSGB10_RING_DIRECT=2
#
# Engine arguments; the defaults in start.sh are the production ones.
# DSGB10_ENGINE_ARGS="--max-ctx 262144"
#
# Images: VISION=1 keeps the encoder's slice of the checkpoint (~2.3 GB) and
# points dsfront at it; VISION_IMAGE is a torch/PIL/safetensors image that runs
# the encoder from that bundle.
# VISION=1
# VISION_IMAGE=<image with torch + PIL + safetensors>
#
# Only for a gated or private checkpoint.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...
#
# Working on the image instead of using it.
# SKIP_BUILD=1
# DRY_RUN=1
